  "无脊椎动物的主要类群有腔肠动物、扁形动物、线形动物、环节动物、软体动物和节肢动物。": "The main groups of invertebrates are cnidarians, flatworms, roundworms, annelids, molluscs and arthropods.",
  "“{0}”是下列哪一类动物的特征？": "“{0}” is a feature of which group of animals?",
  "每一类动物都有各自的主要特征。": "Each group of animals has its own main features.",
  "在脊椎动物的五个类群中，体温恒定的是：": "Among the five groups of vertebrates, those with a constant body temperature are:",
  "鸟类和哺乳动物": "Birds and mammals",
  "鱼类和两栖动物": "Fish and amphibians",
  "两栖动物和爬行动物": "Amphibians and reptiles",
  "鱼类和鸟类": "Fish and birds",
  "爬行动物和哺乳动物": "Reptiles and mammals",
  "鸟类和哺乳动物是恒温动物，其余三类是变温动物。": "Birds and mammals are warm-blooded animals; the other three groups are cold-blooded.",
  "{0}的体表特征是：": "The body covering of {0} is:",
  "体表有外骨骼": "An exoskeleton",
  "体表的覆盖物起保护作用，并与动物的生活环境相适应。": "The covering of the body protects it and suits the animal's habitat.",
  "{0}有几对足？": "How many pairs of legs does {0} have?",
  "昆虫有三对足，蜘蛛有四对足。": "Insects have three pairs of legs, spiders have four pairs.",
  "血压正常": "Normal blood pressure",
  "血压偏高（高血压）": "High blood pressure (hypertension)",
  "血压偏低": "Low blood pressure",
  "甲（正常）": "A (normal)",
  "乙（偏高）": "B (high)",
  "丙（偏低）": "C (low)",
  "袖带压力高于收缩压：血管被压扁，血流被阻断，听不到声音": "Cuff pressure above the systolic pressure: the artery is squeezed shut, the blood flow is blocked, no sound is heard",
  "袖带压力在收缩压和舒张压之间：血流时断时通，能听到脉搏声": "Cuff pressure between the systolic and diastolic pressure: the blood flows on and off, the pulse sound is heard",
  "袖带压力低于舒张压：血流通畅，声音消失": "Cuff pressure below the diastolic pressure: the blood flows freely, the sound disappears",
  "每搏输出量为 {0} mL，心率为 {1} 次/分钟，心输出量约是多少升每分钟？": "The stroke volume is {0} mL and the heart rate {1} beats per minute. About how many litres per minute is the cardiac output?",
  "某人收缩压为 {0} mmHg，舒张压为 {1} mmHg，脉压差是多少？": "A person's systolic pressure is {0} mmHg and diastolic pressure {1} mmHg. What is the pulse pressure?",
  "脉压差 = 收缩压 − 舒张压。": "Pulse pressure = systolic pressure − diastolic pressure.",
  "教科书用 kPa 表示血压。已知 1 kPa = 7.5 mmHg，{0} mmHg 约是多少 kPa？": "Textbooks give blood pressure in kPa. Given 1 kPa = 7.5 mmHg, about how many kPa is {0} mmHg?",
  "kPa 数值 = mmHg 数值 ÷ 7.5。": "Value in kPa = value in mmHg ÷ 7.5.",
  "某人的血压为 {0} / {1} mmHg（收缩压 / 舒张压），属于：": "A person's blood pressure is {0} / {1} mmHg (systolic / diastolic). It is:",
  "健康成年人的收缩压为 90–140 mmHg，舒张压为 60–90 mmHg；超过 140 / 90 mmHg 为偏高。": "In a healthy adult the systolic pressure is 90–140 mmHg and the diastolic pressure 60–90 mmHg; above 140 / 90 mmHg is high.",
  "用袖带测血压时，袖带压力高于收缩压，听诊器里会：": "When measuring blood pressure with a cuff, if the cuff pressure is above the systolic pressure, in the stethoscope you will:",
  "听不到声音，因为血流被阻断": "Hear nothing, because the blood flow is blocked",
  "听到清晰的脉搏声": "Hear a clear pulse sound",
  "听到连续的声音": "Hear a continuous sound",
  "声音突然变大": "Hear the sound suddenly grow louder",
