  "有氧化性": "is oxidising",
  "熟石灰是碱，能与土壤里的酸性物质发生中和反应。": "Slaked lime is a base and undergoes neutralisation with the acidic substances in the soil.",
  "稀盐酸和稀硫酸具有相似的化学性质，是因为它们的溶液中都含有": "Dilute hydrochloric acid and dilute sulfuric acid have similar chemical properties because their solutions both contain",
  "氢离子": "hydrogen ions",
  "氯离子": "chloride ions",
  "硫酸根离子": "sulfate ions",
  "氢氧根离子": "hydroxide ions",
  "酸在水溶液中解离出的阳离子全部是氢离子，所以化学性质相似。": "The only positive ions that an acid releases in water are hydrogen ions, so its chemical properties are similar.",
  "氢氧化钠和氢氧化钙具有相似的化学性质，是因为它们的溶液中都含有": "Sodium hydroxide and calcium hydroxide have similar chemical properties because their solutions both contain",
  "钠离子": "sodium ions",
  "钙离子": "calcium ions",
  "碱在水溶液中解离出的阴离子全部是氢氧根离子。": "The only negative ions that a base releases in water are hydroxide ions.",
  "生活中降低水的硬度常用的方法是": "A common method of lowering the hardness of water at home is",
  "煮沸": "boiling",
  "静置": "leaving it to stand",
  "煮沸使水中的可溶性钙、镁化合物转化为沉淀；实验室用蒸馏。": "Boiling turns the soluble calcium and magnesium compounds in the water into precipitates; the laboratory uses distillation.",
  "区分硬水和软水，可以加入": "To tell hard water from soft water, one can add",
  "酚酞溶液": "phenolphthalein solution",
  "加肥皂水，产生泡沫多的是软水，泡沫少、浮渣多的是硬水。": "Add soapy water: the one that foams a lot is soft water; the one that foams little and gives a lot of scum is hard water.",
  "净化水的方法中，净化程度最高的是": "Of the methods of purifying water, the one that gives the highest degree of purity is",
  "沉淀": "sedimentation",
  "蒸馏得到的是纯水，其他方法不能除去所有可溶性杂质。": "Distillation gives pure water; the other methods cannot remove all the soluble impurities.",
  "元素是具有相同什么的一类原子的总称": "An element is the name for a class of atoms that have the same",
  "核电荷数（质子数）": "nuclear charge (number of protons)",
  "电子数": "number of electrons",
  "元素的种类由质子数（核电荷数）决定，质子数相同的原子属于同一种元素。": "The kind of element is decided by the number of protons (nuclear charge); atoms with the same number of protons belong to the same element.",
  "构成原子的粒子中，不带电的是": "Of the particles that make up an atom, the one that has no charge is the",
  "中子": "neutron",
  "质子": "proton",
  "电子": "electron",
  "原子核": "nucleus",
  "质子带正电，电子带负电，中子不带电；原子核由质子和中子构成，带正电。": "Protons are positive, electrons negative and neutrons neutral; the nucleus is made of protons and neutrons and is positive.",
  "原子的质量主要集中在": "The mass of an atom is mainly concentrated in the",
  "核外空间": "space outside the nucleus",
  "中子和电子": "neutrons and electrons",
  "电子的质量很小，原子的质量主要集中在由质子和中子构成的原子核上。": "The mass of an electron is very small; the mass of an atom is mainly in the nucleus, made of protons and neutrons.",
  "在原子中，下列关系一定成立的是": "In an atom, the relation that always holds is",
  "质子数 = 核外电子数": "number of protons = number of electrons outside the nucleus",
  "质子数 = 中子数": "number of protons = number of neutrons",
