  "太阳的结构": "Structure of the Sun",
  "太阳在这里": "The Sun is here",
  "恒星的一生": "The life of a star",
  "恒星也有出生、成长和结局，质量不同，结局就不同。": "Stars are born, grow up and end, and the end depends on the mass.",
  "像太阳这样的恒星": "Stars like the Sun",
  "质量大得多的恒星": "Much more massive stars",
  "最佳观测：": "Best seen: ",
  "怎样找到：": "How to find it: ",
  "古人把天上的亮星连成图案，编成故事。点开一个星座，看它的名字和故事。图案是示意，不是真实的天空位置。": "People of old joined bright stars into pictures and made up stories. Open a constellation to see its names and its story. The figures are schematic, not the real positions in the sky.",
  "怎样找到北极星": "How to find the Pole Star",
  "先找到北斗七星，它像一把勺子。": "First find the Big Dipper, which looks like a ladle.",
  "勺口外侧的两颗星（天璇、天枢）连成一条线，向勺口方向延长约 5 倍的距离。": "Join the two stars on the outer edge of the bowl and extend the line about 5 times that distance, in the direction of the opening.",
  "那里孤零零的一颗不太亮的星，就是北极星。": "The lonely star of moderate brightness there is the Pole Star.",
  "仙后座的“W”在北极星的另一侧，也能帮助定位。": "The \"W\" of Cassiopeia is on the other side of the Pole Star and helps too.",
  "面对北极星，你就面向正北。": "Facing the Pole Star, you face true north.",
  "从地球到宇宙": "From the Earth to the universe",
  "每一级比上一级大得多。横条的长度按对数画，每多一小格，就是 10 倍。": "Each step is much larger than the one before. The bars are drawn on a logarithmic scale: each small step more means 10 times as much.",
