  "滑动变阻器": "Rheostat",
  "电流表": "Ammeter",
  "电压表": "Voltmeter",
  "电动机": "Motor",
  "导线相连（连接点）": "Wires joined (junction)",
  "导线交叉（不相连）": "Wires crossing (not joined)",
  "简单电路": "A simple circuit",
  "组成：电源、开关、用电器（灯泡）和导线。": "Parts: a source, a switch, a load (lamp) and wires.",
  "电流从电源正极出发，经过用电器，回到电源负极。": "Current leaves the positive pole, goes through the load and returns to the negative pole.",
  "开关闭合，电路是通路，灯亮；开关断开，电路是断路，灯不亮。": "Switch closed: the circuit is complete and the lamp lights. Switch open: the circuit is broken and the lamp is off.",
  "用导线直接连接电源两端，叫短路，会烧坏电源，千万不能这样做。": "Joining the two poles of the source directly with a wire is a short circuit. It can destroy the source: never do it.",
  "串联电路": "Series circuit",
  "用电器首尾依次相连，电流只有一条路径。": "The loads are joined one after another: the current has only one path.",
  "电流处处相等：I = I₁ = I₂。": "The current is the same everywhere: I = I₁ = I₂.",
  "总电压等于各部分电压之和：U = U₁ + U₂。": "The total voltage is the sum of the parts: U = U₁ + U₂.",
  "一个灯坏了（断路），另一个灯也不会亮；开关控制整个电路。": "If one lamp fails (open circuit) the other goes out too; the switch controls the whole circuit.",
  "并联电路": "Parallel circuit",
  "用电器并列地接在电路两点之间，电流有两条（或更多）路径。": "The loads are joined side by side between two points: the current has two (or more) paths.",
  "干路电流等于各支路电流之和：I = I₁ + I₂。": "The main current is the sum of the branch currents: I = I₁ + I₂.",
  "各支路两端的电压相等：U = U₁ = U₂。": "Every branch has the same voltage: U = U₁ = U₂.",
  "一条支路断开，其他支路仍能工作；家里的用电器都是并联的。": "If one branch is cut the others still work; the appliances at home are all in parallel.",
  "电流表和电压表的接法": "Connecting an ammeter and a voltmeter",
  "电流表（A）要串联在被测电路中，电流从“+”接线柱流入、“−”接线柱流出。": "The ammeter (A) goes in series; the current enters at the “+” terminal and leaves at “−”.",
  "电压表（V）要并联在被测用电器两端。": "The voltmeter (V) goes in parallel across the part being measured.",
  "电流表的电阻很小，绝对不能直接接在电源两端（会短路）。": "An ammeter has a very small resistance: never connect it straight across the source (short circuit).",
  "不知道被测值大小时，先用大量程试触，再选合适的量程。": "If you do not know the size of the value, touch with the largest range first, then choose a suitable one.",
  "用滑动变阻器调节灯的亮度": "Dimming a lamp with a rheostat",
  "滑动变阻器要和被控制的灯串联，接线要“一上一下”。": "The rheostat is in series with the lamp; connect “one up, one down”.",
  "滑片移动，改变接入电路的电阻丝的长度，从而改变电阻和电流。": "Moving the slider changes the length of resistance wire in the circuit, so the resistance and the current change.",
  "接入的电阻变大，电流变小，灯变暗；闭合开关前，滑片要放在阻值最大处，保护电路。": "More resistance means less current and a dimmer lamp; before closing the switch put the slider at maximum resistance to protect the circuit.",
  "安培定则（右手螺旋定则）": "Ampère's rule (right-hand screw rule)",
  "用右手握住通电螺线管。": "Grip the solenoid with your right hand.",
  "让四指弯曲的方向和螺线管中的电流方向一致。": "Let the fingers curl in the direction of the current.",
  "大拇指所指的那一端就是螺线管的 N 极。": "The thumb points to the N pole of the solenoid.",
  "改变电流方向，N 极和 S 极也会互换；电流越大、线圈匝数越多，磁性越强。": "Reverse the current and the N and S poles swap; a bigger current and more turns make it stronger.",
  "左手定则（磁场对通电导体的作用力）": "Left-hand rule (force on a current in a magnetic field)",
  "伸出左手，让磁感线（B）垂直穿过手心。": "Hold out your left hand so that the field lines (B) enter the palm.",
  "四指指向电流（I）的方向。": "The fingers point in the direction of the current (I).",
  "大拇指所指的方向，就是通电导体受到的力（F）的方向。": "The thumb gives the direction of the force (F) on the conductor.",
  "电动机的工作原理：通电线圈在磁场中受力转动。电流方向或磁场方向改变，受力方向也随之改变。": "How a motor works: a coil with current turns in a magnetic field. Reverse the current or the field and the force reverses.",
  "右手定则（电磁感应）": "Right-hand rule (electromagnetic induction)",
  "伸出右手，让磁感线（B）垂直穿过手心。": "Hold out your right hand so that the field lines (B) enter the palm.",
  "大拇指指向导体运动的方向（v）。": "The thumb points in the direction the conductor moves (v).",
  "四指所指的方向，就是导体中感应电流（I）的方向。": "The fingers give the direction of the induced current (I).",
  "发电机的工作原理：闭合电路的一部分导体在磁场中做切割磁感线运动，就会产生感应电流（电磁感应）。": "How a generator works: part of a closed circuit cutting the field lines in a magnetic field produces an induced current (electromagnetic induction).",
